                <pb facs="0864" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-25T16:00:00-05:00">February 25, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Your 19, February 21, 4 p.m. I think it very advisable for President Leguia
                    to make the proposition set forth in the report outlined in your 19, February
                    21, 4 p.m. If this is done, I shall strongly urge Chile to accept. Can you tell
                    when President Leguia will make his proposition?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
